GIT:
Git is a version control system.
It keeps track of:
•	What changed
•	Who changed it
•	When it changed
•	Allows going back to older versions
Think of Git as: A camera that takes snapshots of your project.
GITHUB:
Imagine Git is your notebook.
GitHub is the cloud storage where that notebook is stored.
Example
Git = Writing diary at home
GitHub = Keeping a copy online
